3.6.2 Passing the Entire Array
We have discussed that in C the array name refers to the first byte of the array in the memory. 
The address of the remaining elements in the array can be calculated using the array name and 
the index value of the element. Therefore, when we need to pass an entire array to a function, we 
can simply pass the name of the array. Figure 3.22 illustrates the code which passes the entire 
array to the called function.
