5.5  SELF-REFERENTIAL STRUCTURES
Self-referential structures are those structures that contain a reference to the data of its same type. 
That is, a self-referential structure, in addition to other data, contains a pointer to a data that is 
of the same type as that of the structure. For example, consider the structure node given below.
struct node
{
int val;
